 /*
- * Battery-only adaptation of input/negroni_keys.c, observer EXT_READL.
- * PMIC READ ONLY. The only MMIO store issues a one-byte read command.
- * No interrupt clear, peripheral enable, charger config, or PMIC writes.
- * Init is serialized by the single built-in NegroniBattery personality.
- * Battery APIDs are disjoint from the existing keys' 008/4c1 APIDs.
+ * NEGRONI (OnePlus 10 Pro 5G, SM8450): PMIC access for the battery service
+ * (iokit/Kernel/arm/NegroniBattery.cpp), SPMI PMIC arbiter version 7.
+ *
+ * Layout (Linux drivers/spmi/spmi-pmic-arb.c v7; live DT qcom,spmi@c42d000,
+ * qcom,ee = <0>, bus 0 = PMK8350 SID 0 ... PM8350B SID 3 ...):
+ *   core   0x0c400000  version at +0, bus 0 APID count at +4 bits 10:0,
+ *                      APID map at +0x2000 + 4*apid (bits 19:8 = PPID)
+ *   cnfg   0x0c42d000  owner table, 4*apid, bits 2:0 = EE that may write
+ *   obsrvr 0x0c440000  observer (read) channel at 0x8000*ee + 0x20*apid
+ *   chnls  0x0c500000  read/write channel of an APID at 0x1000*apid
+ * Channel registers: CMD +0x00, STATUS +0x08 (bit 0 done, bits 3:1 errors),
+ * WDATA0 +0x10, RDATA0 +0x18. Command: opcode << 27 | reg << 4 | (bytes-1);
+ * EXT_WRITEL = 0, EXT_READL = 1. Same access as negroni_keys.c (keys) and
+ * negroni_reboot.c (patch 0210); each user has its own APIDs, so the
+ * channels do not collide.
+ *
+ * The base tree's version of this file used the sweet (SM6150, arbiter v5)
+ * addresses (core 0x0c440000 = the v7 observer here, observer 0x0e600000)
+ * and refused every arbiter >= 0x70000000, so it never worked on SM8450.
+ *
+ * What may be touched (everything else returns -1):
+ *   read   SID 0 peripheral 0x31 (PMK8350 VADC, ADC7 user channel), any reg
+ *          SID 1/3 offsets 0x04/0x05 (peripheral TYPE/SUBTYPE, census only)
+ *   write  SID 0 0x3140-0x3145, 0x3147: ADC7 APP_SID, DIG_PARAM, FAST_AVG,
+ *          CH_SEL, DELAY, CONV_REQ (Linux adc7_configure), only when the
+ *          owner table gives that APID to EE 0. No charger register, no
+ *          interrupt, no enable bit is ever written.
+ * Callers: thread context, serialized by the NegroniBattery work loop (a lock
+ * is held anyway).
  */
